{"name":"Struck by Lightning","hex":"#f0e1e8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"struck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of strike"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/struck"},{"term":"lightning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flash of light produced by short-duration, high-voltage discharge of electricity within a cloud, between clouds, or between a cloud and the earth.","A discharge of this kind."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extremely fast or sudden; moving (as if) at the speed of lightning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lightning"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lightning strike","blocks":[{"text":"A lightning strike or lightning bolt is a lightning event in which an electric discharge takes place between the atmosphere and the ground. Most originate in a cumulonimbus cloud and terminate on the ground, called cloud-to-ground (CG) lightning. A less common type of strike, ground-to-cloud (GC) lightning, is upward-propagating lightning initiated from a tall grounded object and reaching into the clouds. About 25% of all lightning events worldwide are strikes between the atmosphere and earth-bound objects. Most are intracloud (IC) lightning and cloud-to-cloud (CC), where discharges only occur high in the atmosphere. Lightning strikes the average commercial aircraft at least once a year, but modern engineering and design means this is rarely a problem. The movement of aircraft through clouds can even cause lightning strikes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Rural_nightime_lightning_strike.png/330px-Rural_nightime_lightning_strike.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning_strike"},{"title":"Struck by Lightning (1990 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Struck by Lightning is a 1990 Australian film directed by Jerzy Domaradzki. The film was nominated in 4 AFI Award categories, including Best Director and Best Film. It won the film award at the Human Rights Medal and Awards in 1990."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Struck_by_Lightning_(1990_film)"},{"title":"Struck by Lightning (2012 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Struck by Lightning is a 2012 American coming-of-age comedy drama film directed by Brian Dannelly and written by and starring Chris Colfer. The film had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on 21 April 2012, and was released theatrically on 11 January 2013. It features the final screen appearance of actress Polly Bergen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Struck_By_Lightning_-_Theatrical_Poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Struck_by_Lightning_(2012_film)"},{"title":"Struck","blocks":[{"text":"Struck is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Adolf Struck (1877–1911), German author","Hermann Struck (1876–1944), German artist","Karin Struck (1947–2006), German author","Paul Struck (1776-1820), German composer","Peter Struck (politician) (1943–2012), German politician (SPD)","Peter Struck (classicist), professor at the University of Pennsylvania.","Sille Struck, Danish footballer"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Struck"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Lightning_striking_the_Eiffel_Tower_-_NOAA.jpg/500px-Lightning_striking_the_Eiffel_Tower_-_NOAA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Lightning_striking_the_Eiffel_Tower_-_NOAA.jpg/500px-Lightning_striking_the_Eiffel_Tower_-_NOAA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lightning striking the Eiffel Tower in 1902. The metal tower acts as a colossal lightning conductor. The presence of multiple bolts shows this is a time-exposure photograph","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALightning_striking_the_Eiffel_Tower_-_NOAA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/20150506-LondonGardenMuseum-8.jpg/500px-20150506-LondonGardenMuseum-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/20150506-LondonGardenMuseum-8.jpg/1280px-20150506-LondonGardenMuseum-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/20150506-LondonGardenMuseum-8.jpg/500px-20150506-LondonGardenMuseum-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Memorial to a man killed by lightning in London, 1787","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A20150506-LondonGardenMuseum-8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Lightning_damage.jpg/500px-Lightning_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Lightning_damage.jpg/500px-Lightning_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tree exploded when struck by lightning.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALightning_damage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Lightning_struck_tree_2.jpg/500px-Lightning_struck_tree_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Lightning_struck_tree_2.jpg/1280px-Lightning_struck_tree_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Lightning_struck_tree_2.jpg/500px-Lightning_struck_tree_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This eucalyptus tree was struck by lightning, while two nearby conifers were untouched, Darwin, Northern Territory, Australia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALightning_struck_tree_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/LightningStruckTreeTorontoIslands1991.jpg/500px-LightningStruckTreeTorontoIslands1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/LightningStruckTreeTorontoIslands1991.jpg/1280px-LightningStruckTreeTorontoIslands1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/LightningStruckTreeTorontoIslands1991.jpg/500px-LightningStruckTreeTorontoIslands1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lightning-struck tree in the Toronto Islands, clearly shows the path that the charge took into the ground.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALightningStruckTreeTorontoIslands1991.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Zephyrometer_Lightning_Damage.JPG/500px-Zephyrometer_Lightning_Damage.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Zephyrometer_Lightning_Damage.JPG/1280px-Zephyrometer_Lightning_Damage.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Zephyrometer_Lightning_Damage.JPG/500px-Zephyrometer_Lightning_Damage.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Zephyrometer sculpture in Wellington, New Zealand damaged by lightning","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZephyrometer_Lightning_Damage.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cd/Pointed_Lightning_Rod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca